From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Goyvaerts <jonathan.goyvaerts@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 19:31:33 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] j616: make the headphone jack card the default when
 plugged in

On the J616s (MacBook Pro 16", M4 Pro) the headphone jack is a sound
card of its own, hw:AppleJack (macaudio "MacBook Pro J616 Jack"), apart
from the speaker card: the CS42L84 runs on a different AOP stream, and
a jack codec that never answers must not take the speakers down with
it. UCM's priorities between the jack and the speakers therefore do not
apply across the two cards: nothing orders the jack above the speakers.

Its UCM ties the Headphones and Headset devices to the jack switches,
so unplugged the card has no available profile. Give its nodes
priorities above the J616 speaker filter (priority.session 850) and
the built-in microphones (2000): plugged in, the jack becomes the
default sink and source. A default chosen by hand still wins while it
is available.

Signed-off-by: Jonathan Goyvaerts <jonathan.goyvaerts@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: LLM
(cherry picked from commit a2e263bd24c4a964116517e16e6d3107a9f5a83a)
---
 conf/wireplumber.conf | 30 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 30 insertions(+)

diff --git a/conf/wireplumber.conf b/conf/wireplumber.conf
index c76d857..efdc932 100644
--- a/conf/wireplumber.conf
+++ b/conf/wireplumber.conf
@@ -73,6 +73,36 @@ monitor.alsa.rules = [
             }
         }
     }
+    # J616s: the headphone jack is a card of its own (hw:AppleJack, macaudio
+    # "MacBook Pro J616 Jack"), so UCM's priorities between the jack and the
+    # speakers do not apply across the two cards. Its UCM ties the Headphones
+    # and Headset devices to the jack switches: unplugged, the card has no
+    # available profile. Plugged in, these make the jack the default sink and
+    # source, above the J616 speaker filter (priority.session 850) and the
+    # built-in microphones (2000). A default chosen by hand still wins while
+    # it is available.
+    {
+        matches = [
+            { node.name = "~alsa_output.*", api.alsa.path = "hw:AppleJack,0" }
+        ]
+        actions = {
+            update-props = {
+                priority.driver = 1100
+                priority.session = 1100
+            }
+        }
+    }
+    {
+        matches = [
+            { node.name = "~alsa_input.*", api.alsa.path = "hw:AppleJack,0" }
+        ]
+        actions = {
+            update-props = {
+                priority.driver = 2100
+                priority.session = 2100
+            }
+        }
+    }
 ]
 
 node.software-dsp.rules = [
